Hello World Shortbread.

A shortbread that greets you back. Every quantity in the ingredient list is a
character code, and the method stirs them in backwards - Chef empties a baking
dish from the top down, so the last thing added is the first thing printed.
The flour goes in three times and the almonds twice, because "Hello, World!"
has three l's and two o's, and an ingredient can be reused as often as you
like. Liquefying the bowl at the end is what turns thirteen numbers into
thirteen letters. There is no newline in the list because the interpreter
supplies one; see the README.

Ingredients.
72 g butter
101 g caster sugar
108 g plain flour
111 g ground almonds
44 g cocoa powder
32 g candied peel
87 g mascarpone
114 g dark chocolate
100 g icing sugar
33 g runny honey

Method.
Put runny honey into the mixing bowl.
Put icing sugar into the mixing bowl.
Put plain flour into the mixing bowl.
Put dark chocolate into the mixing bowl.
Put ground almonds into the mixing bowl.
Put mascarpone into the mixing bowl.
Put candied peel into the mixing bowl.
Put cocoa powder into the mixing bowl.
Put ground almonds into the mixing bowl.
Put plain flour into the mixing bowl.
Put plain flour into the mixing bowl.
Put caster sugar into the mixing bowl.
Put butter into the mixing bowl.
Liquefy contents of the mixing bowl.
Pour contents of the mixing bowl into the baking dish.

Serves 1.

